{% import "partials/copy-command.njk" as cmd %}

<h1>Prerequisites</h1>
<p>Three steps, on the controller and on every endpoint. Step 3 is only for remote endpoints.</p>

<h2 id="python">Install Python</h2>
<p>Install Python 3.14 or later from
  <a class="text-accent" href="https://www.python.org/downloads/">python.org</a>. On Windows,
  select <strong>Add python.exe to PATH</strong> in the installer. Then verify:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>OS</th>
      <th>Verify</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Windows</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("python --version") }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Linux, macOS</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("python3 --version") }}</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="virtual-environment">Create a virtual environment</h2>
<p>Run these in the folder you want to work from:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Step</th>
      <th>Windows</th>
      <th>Linux / macOS</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Create</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("python -m venv .venv") }}</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("python3 -m venv .venv") }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Activate</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell(".venv\\Scripts\\activate") }}</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("source .venv/bin/activate") }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Install</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("pip install orcraft") }}</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("pip install orcraft") }}</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Activate the environment in every new terminal before running Orcraft.</p>
<p>If PowerShell blocks the activation script, allow it for the current terminal only:</p>
{{ cmd.copyCommand("Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned") }}

<h2 id="remote-endpoints">Allow remote endpoint traffic (optional)</h2>
<p>Needed only for remote endpoints. On each one, open the port it listens on and allow ping from
  the controller.</p>

<h3 id="tcp-port">Open TCP 50051</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Endpoint OS</th>
      <th>What to do</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Windows</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName 'Orcraft Endpoint' -Direction Inbound -Protocol TCP -LocalPort 50051 -Action Allow") }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Linux with ufw</td>
      <td>{{ cmd.copyCell("sudo ufw allow 50051/tcp") }}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>macOS</td>
      <td>Allow incoming connections when macOS prompts the first time the endpoint runs</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Using a different port? Select it with <code>-port</code>, use that number in the rule, and
  enter the same port when adding the endpoint in the controller.</p>

<h3 id="icmp-ping">Allow ping</h3>
<p>The controller pings each endpoint before connecting to it. Most networks already allow this -
  do this only if an endpoint shows Offline:</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>OS</th>
      <th>What to allow</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Windows</td>
      <td>Inbound "File and Printer Sharing (Echo Request - ICMPv4/ICMPv6)"</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Linux</td>
      <td>ICMP in <code>ufw</code>, <code>firewalld</code>, <code>nftables</code> or
        <code>iptables</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>macOS</td>
      <td>Incoming ping in the firewall; "Block all incoming connections" must be off</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

